      "writtenOn": "2023-02-06T23:08:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we\u0027re conflating \"image\" here with two different concepts. The original `ImageType` allowed toggling between the `RO` and `RW` parts of the test binary (\"image\").\n\nI think we want to be able to independently specify the binary we\u0027re using vs RO/RW. Something like:\n\n```\nclass ImageType(Enum):\n    \"\"\"EC Image type to use for the test.\"\"\"\n    RO \u003d 1\n    RW \u003d 2\n```\n\n```\nclass BinaryType(Enum):\n    TEST \u003d 1\n    PRODUCTION \u003d 2\n```\n\n(Not really happy with `Binary` vs `Image`, so if you can think of better names, feel free to use those.)",
      "parentUuid": "df133bfa_30921937",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 134,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "bae761cb70bbcf533b7602d7956f80155c8af1cb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
